###############################################################################
#  PASSPORT PHOTO CHECKER — DELIVERY PLAN
#  One task = one PR. Branch fresh from `main`. Never start N+1 before N merges.
#  Last updated: 2026-08-28
###############################################################################

═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
 GLOBAL ENGINEERING RULES  (apply to EVERY PR — CI enforces, not reviewers)
═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════

BRANCHING
  - `git checkout main && git pull && git checkout -b <type>/<slug>` for every PR.
  - One PR is never based on another. If N+1 needs N, wait for the merge.
  - Squash-merge only. Branch deleted on merge.

TYPESCRIPT — 100%
  - strict, noUncheckedIndexedAccess, exactOptionalPropertyTypes,
    noImplicitOverride, noFallthroughCasesInSwitch, verbatimModuleSyntax.
  - `any` is a lint error. `as` casts are a lint error except in *.test.ts.
  - Every public function has an explicit return type.
  - Zero `@ts-expect-error` without an issue link in the comment.

FILE LAYOUT — one thing per file
  - One component per file. Component file contains ONLY the component.
  - Props/domain types live in a sibling `*.types.ts`. Never inline interfaces.
  - Constants live in `*.constants.ts`. Pure helpers in `*.utils.ts`.
  - Co-located per component: Foo.tsx, Foo.types.ts, Foo.test.tsx, Foo.stories.tsx
  - BANNED filenames: utils.ts, types.ts, helpers.ts, index.ts re-export barrels.

NO HARDCODED VALUES — anywhere
  - No colour literals in components. Semantic CSS custom properties only.
  - No magic numbers. Thresholds, sizes, timings, limits => *.constants.ts.
  - No route strings. Use typed route builders from routes.constants.ts.
  - No copy strings in components. Pull from a content module (i18n-ready).
  - CI: custom ESLint rules `no-raw-color`, `no-magic-number`, `no-literal-route`.

CSS — one place
  - All tokens in src/styles/tokens.css. Mantine reads them via the
    cssVariablesResolver in src/theme/mantine-theme.config.ts.
  - Component styles are CSS Modules referencing var(--tk-*). No Tailwind.
  - A colour literal outside tokens.css is a stylelint error (color-no-hex).
  - Print styles centralised in src/styles/print.css (this product gets printed).

MANTINE — where it may and may not be used
  - Mantine components are Client Components. Using them for static content
    would ship a hydration bundle for text that never changes and blow the LCP
    budget across the whole ranking surface.
  - USE Mantine for: the checker tool — dropzone, modal, tabs, combobox,
    progress, buttons.
  - DO NOT use Mantine for: headings, body copy, requirements tables, FAQs,
    breadcrumbs, footer links. Those are plain semantic HTML + CSS Modules,
    rendered as Server Components.
  - FAQs are native <details>/<summary>, never a JS accordion — the answer text
    must be in the static HTML and must not cause layout shift.
  - Country navigation is a grid of real <a href>, never a Select that
    navigates. The internal link graph across 150 pages is doing real work.

TESTING — every PR, no exceptions
  - Unit:        Vitest + React Testing Library. 100% statements/branches/
                 functions/lines. CI fails under threshold.
  - A11y:        axe-core assertion in every component test.
  - Storybook:   a story per meaningful state (default, each variant, loading,
                 error, empty, mobile viewport, long-content overflow).
  - Screenshots: Playwright captures every story in every theme and viewport
                 against committed baselines. Zero-pixel tolerance. Diffs fail
                 CI, and expected/actual/diff are written for review.
  - Integration: Playwright specs against real routes, desktop + mobile.
  - Mocking:     MSW for network (model CDN). Fixture-driven fakes for the Web
                 Worker and MediaPipe — see PR #10. There is NO backend API in
                 this product, so the thing that actually needs mocking is the
                 worker + WASM model layer, not HTTP.
  - NOTE: 100% branch coverage on GPU/CPU fallback paths is only reachable
    because of the fake model layer. Any genuinely unreachable branch needs an
    /* c8 ignore */ WITH a comment saying why. Reviewer rejects bare ignores.

SEO — a first-class acceptance criterion, not a follow-up
  - Every route is statically generated (SSG) or ISR. Nothing client-only.
  - Every page: unique <title>, meta description, canonical, OG + Twitter tags.
  - All content that should rank is in the server-rendered HTML. The checker is
    interactive, but the requirements tables, FAQs and source citations are not.
  - All navigation is real <a href>. No JS-only routing for crawlable links.
  - Structured data validated in CI (JSON-LD schema tests).
  - Lighthouse CI budget gate: LCP < 1.2s, CLS < 0.1, TBT < 200ms.
  - PR template has an SEO checklist. Cannot merge unticked.

DEFINITION OF DONE
  [ ] typecheck clean   [ ] lint clean   [ ] unit 100%   [ ] stories added
  [ ] screenshots reviewed   [ ] integration green   [ ] a11y clean
  [ ] SEO checklist ticked   [ ] Lighthouse budgets pass   [ ] docs updated


═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
 SETTLED STACK DECISIONS
═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
  Framework    Next.js 16 App Router, RSC-first, statically generated
  UI library   Mantine 9 (CSS Modules + CSS variables, no runtime CSS-in-JS)
  Styling      CSS Modules + src/styles/tokens.css. NO Tailwind.
  Hosting      Vercel
  Vision       MediaPipe Tasks Vision, behind the swappable detector interface
               from PR #10. If the PR #13 ground-truth set shows segmentation
               failing on dark hair or head coverings, an ONNX model can be
               substituted without touching anything downstream.
  Encoding     jSquash (mozjpeg) for the byte-budget JPEG path
  Validation   Zod 4
  Testing      Vitest + RTL + axe-core · Playwright · Storybook 10 + test-runner
               · MSW for the model CDN


═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
 COMPETITIVE POSITION  (researched August 2026)
═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════

WHO WE ARE AGAINST
  PhotoAiD (passport-photo.online + photoaid.com) — a SERVICE business. $10M
    revenue 2023, 1M+ customers, 11M photos/year, 62-130 staff, founded 2012.
    $16.95 buys human expert review, a 100% acceptance guarantee, double money
    back, prints posted to you. 200+ countries. iOS and Android apps.
  Visafoto — an EDITING business. ~577K visits/month. $6.99-7.99 for AI
    correction: background, crop, tilt, colour, red-eye, 600 DPI, print
    templates. 200+ document types. Refund on proof of rejection.
  IDPhoto4You — an AD business. The largest free player. Crops to a country
    template and stops; its own reviewers note it "won't verify your photo in
    any way against government regulations."

THE GAP, IN ONE SENTENCE
  Free tools crop. Paid tools verify. Nobody does free verification.

WHAT WE WIN ON — three things, not a long list
  1. You find out BEFORE you pay. Even someone who ends up buying from PhotoAiD
     should come to us first, which makes us their top-of-funnel.
  2. The photo never leaves the device. All three upload biometric data. Ours is
     the only trust claim on the page a user can verify in ten seconds.
  3. We show our working — measurement, requirement, source, date, and the
     physical action that fixes it. They give a verdict.

  And one structural advantage nobody can copy: their marginal cost per photo is
  real (GPU time, or a human looking at it). Ours is zero. They cannot match
  free-and-verifying without destroying their own margin.

WHAT WE LOSE ON — say it plainly
  - No acceptance guarantee, and we cannot offer one. Theirs is backed by a
    human who looked at the photo. Ours would be a lie, and "never claim
    acceptance" is a machine-tested invariant. A deliberate disadvantage.
  - No prints, no native apps, no photo enhancement. Each a deliberate no.
  - Zero brand trust against ~700 Trustpilot reviews each. Slowest gap to close.

THE REAL OBSTACLE IS CONTENT, NOT PRODUCT
  PhotoAiD owns the comparison SERP with their own blog. They review the entire
  category on their own domain and rank first for it. That is the single biggest
  thing standing between us and traffic, and no engineering advantage answers it.

REVENUE REALITY — plan against these numbers, not hopes
  Assume ~2.2 pageviews per session and a US/UK/EU audience.
    $1,000/month needs roughly 40-60K sessions/month   -> month 10-14
    $5,000/month needs roughly 150-220K sessions/month -> year 2
  AdSense alone on this audience is realistically $6-10 page RPM. Mediavine
  opens at 50K sessions/month and typically lifts RPM 50-80%, so REACHING 50K
  SESSIONS IS THE HIGHEST-VALUE MILESTONE IN THIS PLAN.

  Affiliate probably beats display for this audience: photo printing, visa
  services, travel insurance. Lead values are $10-50, not fractions of a cent.


