PR #6 — Test fixture corpus and the ground-truth generator
Branch: feat/test-fixtures             Depends on: #5                Status: DONE
───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
DESCRIPTION
  The corpus every later task measures itself against. Pulled ahead of the
  detector work because PR #11's fake backend needs it too, and because the
  dataset licensing question has a decisive answer that shapes the design.

  DECIDED: no real faces, ever. FFHQ is CC BY-NC-SA 4.0 (non-commercial only),
  and CelebA, UTKFace and FairFace carry the same or worse restrictions — all
  unusable in a commercial product. Beyond licensing, committing strangers'
  faces to the repo of a product whose entire pitch is biometric privacy is
  indefensible on its own terms.

IMPLEMENTS
  [x] Tier 1 — programmatic generator. Renders synthetic head silhouettes at
      EXACTLY known crown/chin/eye pixel positions. Ground truth is exact by
      construction rather than hand-measured, so a failing assertion means the
      code is wrong, not that someone mis-measured. Covers the whole geometry
      engine (PR #15) with zero licence risk and kilobytes on disk.
  [~] Tier 2 — SFHQ. DEFERRED to the PR that needs it (#12/#13): the Kaggle
      licence field could not be verified from the build environment, and the
      gate below says confirm in writing before depending on it. Nothing in the
      geometry work needs it.
      Tier 2 — SFHQ (Synthetic Faces High Quality). ~425k StyleGAN2 faces with
      no real person behind any of them, shipping facial landmarks AND face-
      parsing segmentation maps — precisely the ground truth crown detection
      needs and the hardest thing to produce by hand.
      GATE: confirm the Kaggle licence field in writing before depending on it.
  [~] Tier 3 — DEFERRED, needs an access request. Tracked, not built.
      Tier 3 — BioLab-ICAO by request, for offline validation only, never
      committed. 7,740 images ground-truthed against ISO/IEC 19794-5. Publish
      the score; no competitor has that line.
  [x] Hard-case compositor: 12 fixtures covering the documented
      failure modes deterministically from a seed — dark hair on dark
      background, controlled background luminance, head coverings, exposure
      extremes. Do not hope a dataset contains these.
  [x] Manifest schema with pinned SHA-256, size and a REQUIRED licence field;
      integrity verified on every load, not only after download
  [~] Download script itself lands with Tier 2, when there is something to fetch

EDGE CASES
  [x] Licence is a required schema field — an entry without one fails to parse
  [x] Byte-identical across machines — seeded mulberry32, no Math.random,
      asserted by regenerating and comparing every byte
  [~] Skin-tone spread arrives with Tier 2; Tier 1 renders luminance only, so
      the fairness requirement in the exposure work is NOT yet satisfied
  [x] CI needs no network — Tier 1 is generated, never downloaded
  [x] Hash and size checked on load, not only after download
  [x] Truncated buffers degrade rather than throw — a real decode failure mode
  [x] Degenerate specs (zero head width or height) render honest empty frames
      rather than NaN pixels

SEO  n/a

TESTS
  The generator is itself tested: a rendered fixture is measured back and must
  match the parameters it was generated from.

