PR #9 — SEO infrastructure
Branch: feat/seo-infrastructure        Depends on: #5                Status: DONE
───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
DESCRIPTION
  The machinery every page will use. Built before any real page exists, so no
  page can be created without it.

IMPLEMENTS
  [x] buildMetadata() factory — the only way a page gets metadata
  [x] JSON-LD builders: WebApplication, FAQPage, BreadcrumbList, HowTo,
      Organization, each typed and tested
  [x] JsonLdScript — a Server Component, because structured data injected after
      hydration may be read too late or not at all
  [x] app/sitemap.ts, app/robots.ts
  [x] Site origin derived from Vercel automatically; preview deployments are
      forced noindex so a branch build cannot outrank the page it forked
  [ ] Dynamic OG image route — deferred to the country pages, which is the
      first place a per-page image earns its keep
  [ ] hreflang + x-default — deferred until a second locale exists

EDGE CASES
  [x] Canonical is absolute; home returns the bare origin so it agrees with
      trailingSlash:false rather than producing two URLs for one page
  [x] Title and description length warnings, reporting the measured length
  [x] Sitemap throws past 50,000 rather than truncating — a silently shortened
      sitemap stops pages being crawled with no error anywhere
  [x] lastModified is omitted when unknown; defaulting to the build date would
      claim the whole site changed on every deploy
  [x] Utility routes excluded from the sitemap, matching their noindex
  [x] faqJsonLd takes the same FaqEntry array FaqList renders, so structured
      data cannot promise content the reader cannot see
  [x] serialiseJsonLd escapes `<` so a closing tag cannot terminate the script
      element early and inject markup
  [x] robots.txt disallows nothing — blocking a path would also block the
      rendering crawler from fetching the analysis models
  [ ] OG image 404s — the default image asset still needs creating

SEO
  This PR *is* the SEO PR. Add a CI test that curls every built route and
  asserts title, description, canonical and one JSON-LD block are present.

TESTS
  Unit: metadata factory and every JSON-LD builder against schema fixtures.
  Integration: crawl the built output, assert per-route tags.

