PR #36 — Ads integration and launch checklist
Branch: chore/launch                   Depends on: #35               Status: TODO
───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
IMPLEMENTS
  [ ] Ad slots on content pages only, never the checker
  [ ] Affiliate placements, which for this audience likely beat display:
      photo printing on the print sheet, visa services and travel insurance on
      the result page. Lead values in this vertical are $10-50, not fractions
      of a cent, and someone who has just learned their photo passes is in an
      unusually receptive moment.
  [ ] Search Console and sitemap submission; analytics verified
  [ ] Launch content: the 2026 AI-photo-rules explainer
  [ ] Comparison content published by us. PhotoAiD ranks first for "best
      passport photo tool" because they wrote it. We can do the same, and do it
      honestly including where we lose — a real differentiator in a category
      where every comparison is a vendor reviewing itself.
EDGE CASES
  [ ] Ad slots must reserve height or CLS collapses
  [ ] NO ADS ON THE CHECKER PAGE. Not a preference — a hard constraint.
      We invite people to open DevTools and watch the Network tab to verify
      their photo is never uploaded. An ad stack fires dozens of requests to
      unknown third parties, so a visitor doing exactly the verification we
      asked for sees a wall of traffic. That destroys the strongest claim we
      have, on the page where it matters most. Ads live on requirements, FAQ
      and guide pages; the checker stays clean, and its emptiness is part of
      the pitch.
  [ ] AdSense rejects thin tool pages — confirm every route has real content
  [ ] Re-run Lighthouse after ads; budgets still apply
  [ ] Ad-carrying pages are the informational ones, which are also the ones AI
      Overviews are eating. Do not plan the business around display alone.
TESTS  Lighthouse with ads enabled; CLS assertion on ad-bearing routes.


